`},id:1159}),e[1160]=t({parent:e[1159],name:"x",flags:4,mods:32768,cat:0,meta:{desc:`<p>The final X coordinate of the pointer (after modifiers)</p>
`},id:1160}),e[1161]=t({parent:e[1159],name:"y",flags:4,mods:32768,cat:0,meta:{desc:`<p>The final Y coordinate of the pointer (after modifiers)</p>
`},id:1161}),e[1162]=t({parent:e[1159],name:"dx",flags:4,mods:32768,cat:0,meta:{desc:`<p>The horizontal movement of the pointer (after modifiers)</p>
`},id:1162}),e[1163]=t({parent:e[1159],name:"dy",flags:4,mods:32768,cat:0,meta:{desc:`<p>The vertical movement of the pointer (after modifiers).</p>
`},id:1163}),e[1164]=t({parent:e[1159],name:"clientX",flags:32768,mods:32768,cat:0,meta:{desc:`<p>The X coordinate of the pointer in local (DOM content) coordinates.</p>
`},id:1164}),e[1165]=t({parent:e[1159],name:"clientY",flags:32768,mods:32768,cat:0,meta:{desc:`<p>The Y coordinate of the mouse pointer in local (DOM content) coordinates.</p>
`},id:1165}),e[1166]=t({parent:e[1159],name:"active?",flags:32768,mods:32768,cat:0,meta:{desc:`<p>True if touch is still active</p>
`},id:1166}),e[1167]=t({parent:e[1159],name:"ended?",flags:32768,mods:32768,cat:0,meta:{desc:`<p>True if touch has ended</p>
`},id:1167}),e[1168]=t({parent:e[1159],name:"ctrlKey",flags:32768,mods:32768,cat:0,meta:{desc:`<p>Returns true if the <code>control</code> key was down when the mouse event was fired.</p>
`},id:1168}),e[1169]=t({parent:e[1159],name:"altKey",flags:32768,mods:32768,cat:0,meta:{desc:`<p>Returns true if the <code>alt</code> key was down when the mouse event was fired.</p>
`},id:1169}),e[1170]=t({parent:e[1159],name:"shiftKey",flags:32768,mods:32768,cat:0,meta:{desc:`<p>Returns true if the <code>shift</code> key was down when the mouse event was fired.</p>
`},id:1170}),e[1171]=t({parent:e[1159],name:"metaKey",flags:32768,mods:32768,cat:0,meta:{desc:`<p>Returns true if the <code>shift</code> key was down when the mouse event was fired.</p>
`},id:1171}),e[1172]=t({parent:e[1159],name:"pointerType",flags:32768,mods:32768,cat:0,meta:{desc:`<p>Indicates the device type that caused the event (mouse, pen, touch, etc.)</p>
`},id:1172}),e[1173]=t({parent:e[1159],name:"pointerId",flags:32768,mods:32768,cat:0,meta:{summary:"A unique identifier for the pointer causing the event.",desc:`<p>The identifier is unique, being different from the identifiers of all other active pointer events. Since the value may be randomly generated, it is not guaranteed to convey any particular meaning.</p>
`},id:1173}),e[1174]=t({parent:e[1159],name:"@moved",kind:"decorator",flags:8192,mods:32768,cat:1024,meta:{touch:".moved(threshold=4px, dir='any')>\n```",summary:"Only when touch has moved more than threshold",detail:"(threshold = 4px, dir = 'any')",desc:"<p>This guard will break the chain unless the touch has moved more than threshold. Once this threshold has been reached, all subsequent updates of touch will pass through. The element will also activate the <api-link>@move</api-link> pseudostate during touch - after threshold is reached.</p>\n<h4>Syntax</h4><p>```imba\n&lt;div</p>\n",Syntax:!0},id:1174}),e[1175]=t({parent:e[1159],name:"@hold",kind:"decorator",flags:8192,mods:32768,cat:1024,meta:{touch:".hold(duration=250ms)>\n```",summary:"Only start handling after pressing and holding still",detail:"(duration = 250ms)",desc:`<p>This guard will break the chain unless the touch has been held for a duration.
If the pointer moves more than 5px before the modifier activates, the handler will
essentially be cancelled.</p>
<h4>Syntax</h4><p>\`\`\`imba
&lt;div</p>
`,Syntax:!0},id:1175}),e[1176]=t({parent:e[1159],name:"@sync",kind:"decorator",flags:8192,mods:32768,cat:1024,meta:{touch:".sync(target, xprop='x', yprop='y')>\n```",summary:"Sync the x,y properties of touch to another object",detail:"(data, xProp?, yProp?)",desc:"<p>A convenient touch modifier that takes care of updating the x,y values of some data during touch. When touch starts sync will remember the initial x,y values and only add/subtract based on movement of the touch.</p>\n<h4>Syntax</h4><p>```imba\n&lt;div</p>\n",Syntax:!0},id:1176}),e[1177]=t({parent:e[1159],name:"@apply",kind:"decorator",flags:8192,mods:32768,cat:1024,meta:{see:"https",detail:"(data, xProp?, yProp?)",desc:`<p>Sets the x and y properties of object to the x and y properties of touch.</p>
`},id:1177}),e[1178]=t({parent:e[1159],name:"@fit",kind:"decorator",flags:8192,mods:32768,cat:1024,meta:{touch:".fit(target,[xstart,ystart],[xend,yend],snap?)>\n```",summary:"Convert the coordinates of the touch to some other frame of reference.",detail:"(target?,snap?)",desc:"<p>A very common need for touches is to convert the coordinates of the touch to some other frame of reference. When dragging you might want to make x,y relative to the container. For a custom slider you might want to convert the coordinates from pixels to relative offset of the slider track. There are loads of other scenarios where you&#39;d want to convert the coordinates to some arbitrary scale and offset. This can easily be achieved with fitting modifiers.</p>\n<h4>Syntax</h4><p>```imba\n&lt;div</p>\n",Syntax:!0},id:1178}),e[1179]=t({parent:e[1159],name:"@reframe",kind:"decorator",flags:8192,mods:32768,cat:1024,meta:{touch:`.fit but without clamping x,y to the bounds of the
target.`,detail:"(target?, ax?, ay?)",desc:`<p>Just like</p>
`},id:1179}),e[1180]=t({parent:e[1159],name:"@pin",kind:"decorator",flags:8192,mods:32768,cat:1024,meta:{detail:"(target?, ax?, ay?)",desc:`<p>Allow pinning the touch to a certain point in an element, so that
all future x,y values are relative to this pinned point.</p>
`},id:1180}),e[1181]=t({parent:e[1159],name:"@round",kind:"decorator",flags:8192,mods:32768,cat:1024,meta:{detail:"(to = 1)",desc:`<p>Round the x,y coordinates with an optional accuracy</p>
`},id:1181}),e[1182]=t({parent:e[1159],name:"@flag",kind:"decorator",flags:8192,mods:32768,cat:1024,meta:{param:{text:"target",kind:"parameterName"},detail:"(name,target?)",desc:`<p>Add an html class to target for at least 250ms
If the callback returns a promise, the class
will not be removed until said promise has resolved</p>
`},id:1182}),e[1183]=t({parent:e[1159],name:"@primary",kind:"decorator",flags:8192,mods:32768,cat:1024,meta:{desc:`<p>Only trigger if PointerEvent.isPrimary returns true
If pointerType is mouse it will only return true for main mouse button.</p>
`},id:1183}),e[1184]=t({parent:e[1159],name:"@sel",kind:"decorator",flags:8192,mods:32768,cat:1024,meta:{detail:"(selector)",desc:`<p>Only trigger handler if event.target matches selector</p>
`},id:1184}),e[1185]=t({parent:e[1159],name:"@prevent",kind:"decorator",flags:8192,mods:32768,cat:1024,meta:{see:"https",desc:`<p>Tells the browser that the default action should not be taken. The event will still continue to propagate up the tree. See Event.preventDefault()</p>
`},id:1185}),e[1186]=t({parent:e[1159],name:"@stop",kind:"decorator",flags:8192,mods:32768,cat:1024,meta:{desc:`<p>Stops the event from propagating up the tree. Event listeners for the same event on nodes further up the tree will not be triggered. See Event.stopPropagation()</p>
`},id:1186}),e[1187]=t({parent:e[1159],name:"@trap",kind:"decorator",flags:8192,mods:32768,cat:1024,meta:{desc:`<p>Prevents default action &amp; stops event from bubbling.</p>
`},id:1187}),e[1188]=t({parent:e[1159],name:"@self",kind:"decorator",flags:8192,mods:32768,cat:1024,meta:{summary:"Only trigger handler if event.target is the element itself",desc:`<p>The <code>self</code> event modifier is a handy way of reacting to events only when they are clicked on the actual element you are interacting with and not, for example, a child element. This can be useful for things like modal wrappers when you only want to react when clicking directly.</p>
`},id:1188}),e[1189]=t({parent:e[1159],name:"@silent",kind:"decorator",flags:8192,mods:32768,cat:1024,meta:{summary:"Don't trigger imba.commit from this event handler"},id:1189}),e[1190]=t({parent:e[1159],name:"@lock",kind:"decorator",flags:8192,mods:32768,cat:1024,meta:{summary:"Suppress pointer events on all other elements"},id:1190}),e[1191]=t({parent:e[1159],name:"@if",kind:"decorator",flags:8192,mods:32768,cat:1024,meta:{detail:"(condition)",desc:`<p>Only trigger condition is truthy</p>
`},id:1191}),e[1192]=t({parent:e[1158],name:"IntersectRoot",flags:524288,mods:0,cat:0,meta:{},id:1192}),e[1193]=t({parent:e[1158],name:"IntersectOptions",flags:524288,mods:0,cat:0,meta:{},id:1193}),e[1194]=t({parent:e[1158],name:"IntersectEvent",inherits:e[2],flags:32,mods:294912,cat:0,meta:{desc:`<p><a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Intersection_Observer_API">IntersectionObserver</a> is a <a href="https://caniuse.com/#feat=intersectionobserver">well-supported</a> API in modern browsers. It provides a way to asynchronously observe changes in the intersection of a target element with an ancestor element or with a top-level document&#39;s viewport. Imba adds a simplified abstraction on top of this via the custom <api-link>@intersect</api-link> event.</p>
<h4>Syntax</h4><app-code-block data-path="/docs"><code data-name="10.imba" data-lang="imba"># Will only trigger when intersection ratio increases
&lt;div \\@intersect.in=handler&gt;
# Will only trigger when element is more than 50% visible
&lt;div \\@intersect(0.5).in=handler&gt;</code></app-code-block><h4>Parameters</h4><p>The <api-link>@intersect</api-link> events accepts several arguments. You can pass in an object with the same <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/IntersectionObserver/root">root</a>, <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/IntersectionObserver/rootMargin">rootMargin</a>, and <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/IntersectionObserver/threshold">threshold</a>  properties supported by <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/IntersectionObserver/IntersectionObserver">IntersectionObserver</a>.</p>
<app-code-block data-path="/docs"><code data-name="11.imba" data-lang="imba">&lt;div \\@intersect=handler&gt; # default options
&lt;div \\@intersect(root: frame, rootMargin: '20px')=handler&gt;
&lt;div \\@intersect(threshold: [0,0.5,1])=handler&gt;</code></app-code-block><p>For convenience, imba will convert certain arguments into options. A single number between 0 and 1 will map to the <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/IntersectionObserver/threshold">threshold</a> option:</p>
<app-code-block data-path="/docs"><code data-name="12.imba" data-lang="imba"># n 0-1 adds single threshold at n visibility
&lt;div \\@intersect(0)=handler&gt; # {threshold: 0}
&lt;div \\@intersect(0.5)=handler&gt; # {threshold: 0.5}
&lt;div \\@intersect(1)=handler&gt; # {threshold: 1.0}</code></app-code-block><p>Any number above 1 will add n thresholds, spread evenly:</p>
<app-code-block data-path="/docs"><code data-name="13.imba" data-lang="imba">&lt;div \\@intersect(2)=handler&gt; # {threshold: [0,1]}
&lt;div \\@intersect(3)=handler&gt; # {threshold: [0,0.5,1]}
&lt;div \\@intersect(5)=handler&gt; # {threshold: [0,0.25,0.5,0.75,1]}
# ... and so forth</code></app-code-block><p>An element will map to the <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/IntersectionObserver/root">root</a> option:</p>
<app-code-block data-path="/docs"><code data-name="14.imba" data-lang="imba">&lt;div \\@intersect(frame)=handler&gt; # {root: frame}
&lt;div \\@intersect(frame,3)=handler&gt; # {root: frame, threshold: [0,0.5,1]}</code></app-code-block><p>A string will map to the <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/IntersectionObserver/rootMargin">rootMargin</a> option:</p>
<app-code-block data-path="/docs"><code data-name="15.imba" data-lang="imba">&lt;div \\@intersect("20px 10px")=handler&gt; # {rootMargin: "20px 10px"}</code></app-code-block>`,Syntax:!0,Parameters:!0},id:1194}),e[1195]=t({parent:e[1194],name:"@in",kind:"modifier",flags:268435456,mods:32768,cat:0,meta:{summary:"Stop handling unless intersectionRatio has increased.",desc:`<p>The <code>out</code> modifier stops the handler unless intersectionRatio has <em>increased</em>.</p>
<h4>Syntax</h4><app-code-block data-path="/docs"><code data-name="23.imba" data-lang="imba"># Will only trigger when intersection ratio increases
&lt;div \\@intersect.in=handler&gt;
# Will only trigger when element is more than 50% visible
&lt;div \\@intersect(0.5).in=handler&gt;</code></app-code-block>`,Syntax:!0},id:1195}),e[1196]=t({parent:e[1194],name:"@out",kind:"modifier",flags:268435456,mods:32768,cat:0,meta:{summary:"Stop handling unless intersectionRatio has decreased.",desc:`<p>The <code>out</code> modifier stops the handler unless intersectionRatio has <em>decreased</em>.</p>
<h4>Syntax</h4><app-code-block data-path="/docs"><code data-name="26.imba" data-lang="imba"># Will only trigger when element starts intersecting
&lt;div \\@intersect.out=handler&gt;
# Will trigger whenever any part of the div is hidden
&lt;div \\@intersect(1).out=handler&gt;</code></app-code-block>`,Syntax:!0},id:1196}),e[1197]=t({parent:e[1194],name:"@css",kind:"modifier",flags:268435456,mods:32768,cat:0,meta:{summary:"Set css variable `--ratio` to the intersectionRatio.",desc:`<p>The css modifier sets a css variable --ratio on the event target with the current ratio.</p>
`},id:1197}),e[1198]=t({parent:e[1194],name:"@flag",kind:"modifier",flags:268435456,mods:32768,cat:0,meta:{param:{text:"name",kind:"parameterName"},desc:`<p>Will add a class to the DOM element when intersecting</p>
`},id:1198}),e[1199]=t({parent:e[1194],name:"@options",kind:"modifier",flags:268435456,mods:32768,cat:0,meta:{param:{text:"thresholds",kind:"parameterName"},desc:`<p>Configuring</p>
`},id:1199}),e[1201]=t({parent:e[1],name:"IntersectionObserverEntry",flags:65,mods:0,cat:0,meta:{desc:`<p>This Intersection Observer API interface describes the intersection between the target element and its root container at a specific moment of transition.</p>
`,dom:!0},id:1201}),e[1200]=t({parent:e[1194],name:"entry",flags:4,mods:32768,cat:0,meta:{desc:`<p>The raw IntersectionObserverEntry</p>
`},id:1200,valuetype:e[1201]}),e[1203]=t({parent:e[1],name:"DOMRectReadOnly",flags:65,mods:0,cat:0,meta:{dom:!0},id:1203}),e[1202]=t({parent:e[1201],name:"boundingClientRect",flags:4,mods:8,cat:0,meta:{dom:!0},id:1202,valuetype:e[1203]}),e[1204]=t({parent:e[1203],name:"bottom",flags:4,mods:8,cat:0,meta:{dom:!0},id:1204}),e[1205]=t({parent:e[1203],name:"height",flags:4,mods:8,cat:0,meta:{dom:!0},id:1205}),e[1206]=t({parent:e[1203],name:"left",flags:4,mods:8,cat:0,meta:{dom:!0},id:1206}),e[1207]=t({parent:e[1203],name:"right",flags:4,mods:8,cat:0,meta:{dom:!0},id:1207}),e[1208]=t({parent:e[1203],name:"top",flags:4,mods:8,cat:0,meta:{dom:!0},id:1208}),e[1209]=t({parent:e[1203],name:"width",flags:4,mods:8,cat:0,meta:{dom:!0},id:1209}),e[1210]=t({parent:e[1203],name:"x",flags:4,mods:8,cat:0,meta:{dom:!0},id:1210}),e[1211]=t({parent:e[1203],name:"y",flags:4,mods:8,cat:0,meta:{dom:!0},id:1211}),e[1212]=t({parent:e[1203],name:"toJSON",flags:8192,mods:0,cat:0,meta:{dom:!0},id:1212}),e[1213]=t({parent:e[1201],name:"intersectionRatio",flags:4,mods:8,cat:0,meta:{dom:!0},id:1213}),e[1214]=t({parent:e[1201],name:"intersectionRect",flags:4,mods:8,cat:0,meta:{dom:!0},id:1214,valuetype:e[1203]}),e[1215]=t({parent:e[1201],name:"isIntersecting",flags:4,mods:8,cat:0,meta:{dom:!0},id:1215}),e[1216]=t({parent:e[1201],name:"rootBounds",flags:4,mods:8,cat:0,meta:{dom:!0},id:1216,valuetype:e[1203]}),e[1217]=t({parent:e[1201],name:"target",flags:4,mods:524296,cat:0,meta:{dom:!0},id:1217,valuetype:e[107]}),e[1218]=t({parent:e[1201],name:"time",flags:4,mods:8,cat:0,meta:{dom:!0},id:1218}),e[1219]=t({parent:e[1194],name:"ratio",flags:4,mods:32768,cat:0,meta:{desc:`<p>Ratio of the intersectionRect to the boundingClientRect</p>
`},id:1219}),e[1220]=t({parent:e[1194],name:"delta",flags:4,mods:32768,cat:0,meta:{desc:`<p>Difference in ratio since previous event</p>
`},id:1220}),e[1221]=t({parent:e[1158],name:"ResizeEvent",inherits:e[44],flags:32,mods:294912,cat:0,meta:{desc:`<p>The <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/ResizeObserver">ResizeObserver</a> interface reports changes to the dimensions of an Element&#39;s content or border box. It has <a href="https://caniuse.com/#feat=resizeobserver">good browser support</a> and is very useful in a wide variety of usecases. ResizeObserver avoids infinite callback loops and cyclic dependencies that are often created when resizing via a callback function. It does this by only processing elements deeper in the DOM in subsequent frames.</p>
`},id:1221}),e[1222]=t({parent:e[1221],name:"width",flags:4,mods:32776,cat:0,meta:{desc:`<p>Width of the resized element</p>
