`,aliases:["p"]},id:2770}),e[2771]=t({parent:e[2353],name:"position",flags:4,mods:0,cat:2,meta:{alias:"pos",desc:`<p>The position CSS property sets how an element is positioned in a document. The top, right, bottom, and left properties determine the final location of positioned elements.</p>
`,aliases:["pos"]},id:2771}),e[2772]=t({parent:e[2771],name:"absolute",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>The box&#39;s position (and possibly size) is specified with the &#39;top&#39;, &#39;right&#39;, &#39;bottom&#39;, and &#39;left&#39; properties. These properties specify offsets with respect to the box&#39;s &#39;containing block&#39;.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2772}),e[2773]=t({parent:e[2771],name:"fixed",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>The box&#39;s position is calculated according to the &#39;absolute&#39; model, but in addition, the box is fixed with respect to some reference. As with the &#39;absolute&#39; model, the box&#39;s margins do not collapse with any other margins.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2773}),e[2774]=t({parent:e[2771],name:"-ms-page",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>The box&#39;s position is calculated according to the &#39;absolute&#39; model.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2774}),e[2775]=t({parent:e[2771],name:"relative",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>The box&#39;s position is calculated according to the normal flow (this is called the position in normal flow). Then the box is offset relative to its normal position.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2775}),e[2776]=t({parent:e[2771],name:"static",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>The box is a normal box, laid out according to the normal flow. The &#39;top&#39;, &#39;right&#39;, &#39;bottom&#39;, and &#39;left&#39; properties do not apply.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2776}),e[2777]=t({parent:e[2771],name:"sticky",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>The box&#39;s position is calculated according to the normal flow. Then the box is offset relative to its flow root and containing block and in all cases, including table elements, does not affect the position of any following boxes.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2777}),e[2778]=t({parent:e[2771],name:"-webkit-sticky",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>The box&#39;s position is calculated according to the normal flow. Then the box is offset relative to its flow root and containing block and in all cases, including table elements, does not affect the position of any following boxes.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2778}),e[2779]=t({parent:e[2353],name:"border",flags:4,mods:0,cat:2,meta:{alias:"bd",desc:`<p>Shorthand property for setting border width, style, and color.</p>
`,aliases:["bd"]},id:2779}),e[2780]=t({parent:e[2353],name:"margin",flags:4,mods:0,cat:2,meta:{alias:"m",desc:`<p>Shorthand property to set values the thickness of the margin area. If left is omitted, it is the same as right. If bottom is omitted it is the same as top, if right is omitted it is the same as top. Negative values for margin properties are allowed, but there may be implementation-specific limits.</p>
`,aliases:["m"]},id:2780}),e[2781]=t({parent:e[2353],name:"svg",flags:4,mods:0,cat:2,meta:{desc:`<p>Set asset as inline background svg</p>
`},id:2781}),e[2782]=t({parent:e[2353],name:"top",flags:4,mods:0,cat:2,meta:{alias:"t",desc:`<p>Specifies how far an absolutely positioned box&#39;s top margin edge is offset below the top edge of the box&#39;s &#39;containing block&#39;.</p>
`,aliases:["t"]},id:2782}),e[2783]=t({parent:e[2782],name:"auto",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>For non-replaced elements, the effect of this value depends on which of related properties have the value &#39;auto&#39; as well</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2783}),e[2784]=t({parent:e[2353],name:"left",flags:4,mods:0,cat:2,meta:{alias:"l",desc:`<p>Specifies how far an absolutely positioned box&#39;s left margin edge is offset to the right of the left edge of the box&#39;s &#39;containing block&#39;.</p>
`,aliases:["l"]},id:2784}),e[2785]=t({parent:e[2784],name:"auto",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>For non-replaced elements, the effect of this value depends on which of related properties have the value &#39;auto&#39; as well</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2785}),e[2786]=t({parent:e[2353],name:"margin-top",flags:4,mods:0,cat:2,meta:{alias:"mt",desc:`<p>Shorthand property to set values the thickness of the margin area. If left is omitted, it is the same as right. If bottom is omitted it is the same as top, if right is omitted it is the same as top. Negative values for margin properties are allowed, but there may be implementation-specific limits..</p>
`,aliases:["mt"]},id:2786}),e[2787]=t({parent:e[2353],name:"color",flags:4,mods:0,cat:2,meta:{alias:"c",desc:`<p>Sets the color of an element&#39;s text</p>
`,aliases:["c"]},id:2787}),e[2788]=t({parent:e[2353],name:"font-size",flags:4,mods:0,cat:2,meta:{alias:"fs",desc:`<p>Indicates the desired height of glyphs from the font. For scalable fonts, the font-size is a scale factor applied to the EM unit of the font. (Note that certain glyphs may bleed outside their EM box.) For non-scalable fonts, the font-size is converted into absolute units and matched against the declared font-size of the font, using the same absolute coordinate space for both of the matched values.</p>
`,aliases:["fs"]},id:2788}),e[2789]=t({parent:e[2353],name:"background-color",flags:4,mods:0,cat:2,meta:{alias:"bgc",desc:`<p>Sets the background color of an element.</p>
`,aliases:["bgc"]},id:2789}),e[2790]=t({parent:e[2353],name:"text-align",flags:4,mods:0,cat:2,meta:{alias:"ta",desc:`<p>Describes how inline contents of a block are horizontally aligned if the contents do not completely fill the line box.</p>
`,aliases:["ta"]},id:2790}),e[2791]=t({parent:e[2790],name:"center",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>The inline contents are centered within the line box.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2791}),e[2792]=t({parent:e[2790],name:"end",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>The inline contents are aligned to the end edge of the line box.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2792}),e[2793]=t({parent:e[2790],name:"justify",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>The text is justified according to the method specified by the &#39;text-justify&#39; property.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2793}),e[2794]=t({parent:e[2790],name:"left",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>The inline contents are aligned to the left edge of the line box. In vertical text, &#39;left&#39; aligns to the edge of the line box that would be the start edge for left-to-right text.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2794}),e[2795]=t({parent:e[2790],name:"right",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>The inline contents are aligned to the right edge of the line box. In vertical text, &#39;right&#39; aligns to the edge of the line box that would be the end edge for left-to-right text.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2795}),e[2796]=t({parent:e[2790],name:"start",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>The inline contents are aligned to the start edge of the line box.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2796}),e[2797]=t({parent:e[2353],name:"opacity",flags:4,mods:0,cat:2,meta:{alias:"o",desc:`<p>Opacity of an element&#39;s text, where 1 is opaque and 0 is entirely transparent.</p>
`,aliases:["o"]},id:2797}),e[2798]=t({parent:e[2353],name:"background",flags:4,mods:0,cat:2,meta:{alias:"bg",desc:`<p>Shorthand property for setting most background properties at the same place in the style sheet.</p>
`,aliases:["bg"]},id:2798}),e[2799]=t({parent:e[2798],name:"fixed",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>The background is fixed with regard to the viewport. In paged media where there is no viewport, a &#39;fixed&#39; background is fixed with respect to the page box and therefore replicated on every page.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2799}),e[2800]=t({parent:e[2798],name:"local",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>The background is fixed with regard to the element&#39;s contents: if the element has a scrolling mechanism, the background scrolls with the element&#39;s contents.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2800}),e[2801]=t({parent:e[2798],name:"none",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>A value of &#39;none&#39; counts as an image layer but draws nothing.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2801}),e[2802]=t({parent:e[2798],name:"scroll",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>The background is fixed with regard to the element itself and does not scroll with its contents. (It is effectively attached to the element&#39;s border.)</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2802}),e[2803]=t({parent:e[2353],name:"font-weight",flags:4,mods:0,cat:2,meta:{alias:"fw",desc:`<p>Specifies weight of glyphs in the font, their degree of blackness or stroke thickness.</p>
`,aliases:["fw"]},id:2803}),e[2804]=t({parent:e[2803],name:"100",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>Thin</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2804}),e[2805]=t({parent:e[2803],name:"200",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>Extra Light (Ultra Light)</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2805}),e[2806]=t({parent:e[2803],name:"300",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>Light</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2806}),e[2807]=t({parent:e[2803],name:"400",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>Normal</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2807}),e[2808]=t({parent:e[2803],name:"500",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>Medium</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2808}),e[2809]=t({parent:e[2803],name:"600",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>Semi Bold (Demi Bold)</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2809}),e[2810]=t({parent:e[2803],name:"700",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>Bold</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2810}),e[2811]=t({parent:e[2803],name:"800",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>Extra Bold (Ultra Bold)</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2811}),e[2812]=t({parent:e[2803],name:"900",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>Black (Heavy)</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2812}),e[2813]=t({parent:e[2803],name:"bold",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>Same as 700</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2813}),e[2814]=t({parent:e[2803],name:"bolder",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>Specifies the weight of the face bolder than the inherited value.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2814}),e[2815]=t({parent:e[2803],name:"lighter",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>Specifies the weight of the face lighter than the inherited value.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2815}),e[2816]=t({parent:e[2803],name:"normal",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>Same as 400</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2816}),e[2817]=t({parent:e[2353],name:"overflow",flags:4,mods:0,cat:2,meta:{alias:"of",desc:`<p>Shorthand for setting &#39;overflow-x&#39; and &#39;overflow-y&#39;.</p>
`,aliases:["of"]},id:2817}),e[2818]=t({parent:e[2817],name:"auto",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>The behavior of the &#39;auto&#39; value is UA-dependent, but should cause a scrolling mechanism to be provided for overflowing boxes.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2818}),e[2819]=t({parent:e[2817],name:"hidden",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>Content is clipped and no scrolling mechanism should be provided to view the content outside the clipping region.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2819}),e[2820]=t({parent:e[2817],name:"-moz-hidden-unscrollable",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>Same as the standardized &#39;clip&#39;, except doesn’t establish a block formatting context.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2820}),e[2821]=t({parent:e[2817],name:"scroll",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>Content is clipped and if the user agent uses a scrolling mechanism that is visible on the screen (such as a scroll bar or a panner), that mechanism should be displayed for a box whether or not any of its content is clipped.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2821}),e[2822]=t({parent:e[2817],name:"visible",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>Content is not clipped, i.e., it may be rendered outside the content box.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2822}),e[2823]=t({parent:e[2353],name:"font-family",flags:4,mods:0,cat:2,meta:{alias:"ff",desc:`<p>Specifies a prioritized list of font family names or generic family names. A user agent iterates through the list of family names until it matches an available font that contains a glyph for the character to be rendered.</p>
`,aliases:["ff"]},id:2823}),e[2824]=t({parent:e[2353],name:"float",flags:4,mods:0,cat:2,meta:{desc:`<p>Specifies how a box should be floated. It may be set for any element, but only applies to elements that generate boxes that are not absolutely positioned.</p>
`},id:2824}),e[2825]=t({parent:e[2824],name:"inline-end",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>A keyword indicating that the element must float on the end side of its containing block. That is the right side with ltr scripts, and the left side with rtl scripts.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2825}),e[2826]=t({parent:e[2824],name:"inline-start",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>A keyword indicating that the element must float on the start side of its containing block. That is the left side with ltr scripts, and the right side with rtl scripts.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2826}),e[2827]=t({parent:e[2824],name:"left",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>The element generates a block box that is floated to the left. Content flows on the right side of the box, starting at the top (subject to the &#39;clear&#39; property).</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2827}),e[2828]=t({parent:e[2824],name:"none",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>The box is not floated.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2828}),e[2829]=t({parent:e[2824],name:"right",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>Similar to &#39;left&#39;, except the box is floated to the right, and content flows on the left side of the box, starting at the top.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2829}),e[2830]=t({parent:e[2353],name:"line-height",flags:4,mods:0,cat:2,meta:{alias:"lh",desc:`<p>Determines the block-progression dimension of the text content area of an inline box.</p>
`,aliases:["lh"]},id:2830}),e[2831]=t({parent:e[2830],name:"normal",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>Tells user agents to set the computed value to a &#39;reasonable&#39; value based on the font size of the element.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2831}),e[2832]=t({parent:e[2353],name:"box-sizing",flags:4,mods:0,cat:2,meta:{desc:`<p>Specifies the behavior of the &#39;width&#39; and &#39;height&#39; properties.</p>
`},id:2832}),e[2833]=t({parent:e[2832],name:"border-box",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>The specified width and height (and respective min/max properties) on this element determine the border box of the element.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2833}),e[2834]=t({parent:e[2832],name:"content-box",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>Behavior of width and height as specified by CSS2.1. The specified width and height (and respective min/max properties) apply to the width and height respectively of the content box of the element.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2834}),e[2835]=t({parent:e[2353],name:"text-decoration",flags:4,mods:0,cat:2,meta:{alias:"td",desc:`<p>Decorations applied to font used for an element&#39;s text.</p>
`,aliases:["td"]},id:2835}),e[2836]=t({parent:e[2835],name:"dashed",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>Produces a dashed line style.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2836}),e[2837]=t({parent:e[2835],name:"dotted",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>Produces a dotted line.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2837}),e[2838]=t({parent:e[2835],name:"double",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>Produces a double line.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2838}),e[2839]=t({parent:e[2835],name:"line-through",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>Each line of text has a line through the middle.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2839}),e[2840]=t({parent:e[2835],name:"none",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>Produces no line.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2840}),e[2841]=t({parent:e[2835],name:"overline",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>Each line of text has a line above it.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2841}),e[2842]=t({parent:e[2835],name:"solid",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>Produces a solid line.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2842}),e[2843]=t({parent:e[2835],name:"underline",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>Each line of text is underlined.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2843}),e[2844]=t({parent:e[2835],name:"wavy",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>Produces a wavy line.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2844}),e[2845]=t({parent:e[2353],name:"z-index",flags:4,mods:0,cat:2,meta:{alias:"zi",desc:`<p>For a positioned box, the &#39;z-index&#39; property specifies the stack level of the box in the current stacking context and whether the box establishes a local stacking context.</p>
`,aliases:["zi"]},id:2845}),e[2846]=t({parent:e[2845],name:"auto",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>The stack level of the generated box in the current stacking context is 0. The box does not establish a new stacking context unless it is the root element.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2846}),e[2847]=t({parent:e[2353],name:"vertical-align",flags:4,mods:0,cat:2,meta:{alias:"va",desc:`<p>Affects the vertical positioning of the inline boxes generated by an inline-level element inside a line box.</p>
`,aliases:["va"]},id:2847}),e[2848]=t({parent:e[2847],name:"auto",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>Align the dominant baseline of the parent box with the equivalent, or heuristically reconstructed, baseline of the element inline box.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2848}),e[2849]=t({parent:e[2847],name:"baseline",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>Align the &#39;alphabetic&#39; baseline of the element with the &#39;alphabetic&#39; baseline of the parent element.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2849}),e[2850]=t({parent:e[2847],name:"bottom",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>Align the after edge of the extended inline box with the after-edge of the line box.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2850}),e[2851]=t({parent:e[2847],name:"middle",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>Align the &#39;middle&#39; baseline of the inline element with the middle baseline of the parent.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2851}),e[2852]=t({parent:e[2847],name:"sub",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>Lower the baseline of the box to the proper position for subscripts of the parent&#39;s box. (This value has no effect on the font size of the element&#39;s text.)</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2852}),e[2853]=t({parent:e[2847],name:"super",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>Raise the baseline of the box to the proper position for superscripts of the parent&#39;s box. (This value has no effect on the font size of the element&#39;s text.)</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2853}),e[2854]=t({parent:e[2847],name:"text-bottom",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>Align the bottom of the box with the after-edge of the parent element&#39;s font.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2854}),e[2855]=t({parent:e[2847],name:"text-top",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>Align the top of the box with the before-edge of the parent element&#39;s font.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2855}),e[2856]=t({parent:e[2847],name:"top",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>Align the before edge of the extended inline box with the before-edge of the line box.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2856}),e[2857]=t({parent:e[2353],name:"cursor",flags:4,mods:0,cat:2,meta:{desc:`<p>Allows control over cursor appearance in an element</p>
`},id:2857}),e[2858]=t({parent:e[2857],name:"alias",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>Indicates an alias of/shortcut to something is to be created. Often rendered as an arrow with a small curved arrow next to it.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2858}),e[2859]=t({parent:e[2857],name:"all-scroll",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>Indicates that the something can be scrolled in any direction. Often rendered as arrows pointing up, down, left, and right with a dot in the middle.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2859}),e[2860]=t({parent:e[2857],name:"auto",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>The UA determines the cursor to display based on the current context.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2860}),e[2861]=t({parent:e[2857],name:"cell",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>Indicates that a cell or set of cells may be selected. Often rendered as a thick plus-sign with a dot in the middle.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2861}),e[2862]=t({parent:e[2857],name:"col-resize",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>Indicates that the item/column can be resized horizontally. Often rendered as arrows pointing left and right with a vertical bar separating them.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2862}),e[2863]=t({parent:e[2857],name:"context-menu",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>A context menu is available for the object under the cursor. Often rendered as an arrow with a small menu-like graphic next to it.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2863}),e[2864]=t({parent:e[2857],name:"copy",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>Indicates something is to be copied. Often rendered as an arrow with a small plus sign next to it.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2864}),e[2865]=t({parent:e[2857],name:"crosshair",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>A simple crosshair (e.g., short line segments resembling a &#39;+&#39; sign). Often used to indicate a two dimensional bitmap selection mode.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2865}),e[2866]=t({parent:e[2857],name:"default",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>The platform-dependent default cursor. Often rendered as an arrow.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2866}),e[2867]=t({parent:e[2857],name:"e-resize",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>Indicates that east edge is to be moved.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2867}),e[2868]=t({parent:e[2857],name:"ew-resize",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>Indicates a bidirectional east-west resize cursor.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2868}),e[2869]=t({parent:e[2857],name:"grab",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>Indicates that something can be grabbed.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2869}),e[2870]=t({parent:e[2857],name:"grabbing",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>Indicates that something is being grabbed.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2870}),e[2871]=t({parent:e[2857],name:"help",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>Help is available for the object under the cursor. Often rendered as a question mark or a balloon.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2871}),e[2872]=t({parent:e[2857],name:"move",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>Indicates something is to be moved.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2872}),e[2873]=t({parent:e[2857],name:"-moz-grab",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>Indicates that something can be grabbed.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2873}),e[2874]=t({parent:e[2857],name:"-moz-grabbing",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>Indicates that something is being grabbed.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2874}),e[2875]=t({parent:e[2857],name:"-moz-zoom-in",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>Indicates that something can be zoomed (magnified) in.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2875}),e[2876]=t({parent:e[2857],name:"-moz-zoom-out",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>Indicates that something can be zoomed (magnified) out.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2876}),e[2877]=t({parent:e[2857],name:"ne-resize",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>Indicates that movement starts from north-east corner.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2877}),e[2878]=t({parent:e[2857],name:"nesw-resize",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>Indicates a bidirectional north-east/south-west cursor.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2878}),e[2879]=t({parent:e[2857],name:"no-drop",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>Indicates that the dragged item cannot be dropped at the current cursor location. Often rendered as a hand or pointer with a small circle with a line through it.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2879}),e[2880]=t({parent:e[2857],name:"none",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>No cursor is rendered for the element.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2880}),e[2881]=t({parent:e[2857],name:"not-allowed",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>Indicates that the requested action will not be carried out. Often rendered as a circle with a line through it.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2881}),e[2882]=t({parent:e[2857],name:"n-resize",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>Indicates that north edge is to be moved.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2882}),e[2883]=t({parent:e[2857],name:"ns-resize",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>Indicates a bidirectional north-south cursor.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2883}),e[2884]=t({parent:e[2857],name:"nw-resize",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>Indicates that movement starts from north-west corner.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2884}),e[2885]=t({parent:e[2857],name:"nwse-resize",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>Indicates a bidirectional north-west/south-east cursor.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2885}),e[2886]=t({parent:e[2857],name:"pointer",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>The cursor is a pointer that indicates a link.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2886}),e[2887]=t({parent:e[2857],name:"progress",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>A progress indicator. The program is performing some processing, but is different from &#39;wait&#39; in that the user may still interact with the program. Often rendered as a spinning beach ball, or an arrow with a watch or hourglass.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2887}),e[2888]=t({parent:e[2857],name:"row-resize",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>Indicates that the item/row can be resized vertically. Often rendered as arrows pointing up and down with a horizontal bar separating them.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2888}),e[2889]=t({parent:e[2857],name:"se-resize",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>Indicates that movement starts from south-east corner.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2889}),e[2890]=t({parent:e[2857],name:"s-resize",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>Indicates that south edge is to be moved.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2890}),e[2891]=t({parent:e[2857],name:"sw-resize",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>Indicates that movement starts from south-west corner.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2891}),e[2892]=t({parent:e[2857],name:"text",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>Indicates text that may be selected. Often rendered as a vertical I-beam.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2892}),e[2893]=t({parent:e[2857],name:"vertical-text",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>Indicates vertical-text that may be selected. Often rendered as a horizontal I-beam.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2893}),e[2894]=t({parent:e[2857],name:"wait",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>Indicates that the program is busy and the user should wait. Often rendered as a watch or hourglass.</p>
