`},id:2921}),e[2922]=t({parent:e[2921],name:"attr",flags:8192,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>The attr(n) function returns as a string the value of attribute n for the subject of the selector.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2922}),e[2923]=t({parent:e[2921],name:"counter",flags:8192,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>Counters are denoted by identifiers (see the &#39;counter-increment&#39; and &#39;counter-reset&#39; properties).</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2923}),e[2924]=t({parent:e[2921],name:"icon",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>The (pseudo-)element is replaced in its entirety by the resource referenced by its &#39;icon&#39; property, and treated as a replaced element.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2924}),e[2925]=t({parent:e[2921],name:"none",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>On elements, this inhibits the children of the element from being rendered as children of this element, as if the element was empty. On pseudo-elements it causes the pseudo-element to have no content.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2925}),e[2926]=t({parent:e[2921],name:"normal",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>See <a href="http://www.w3.org/TR/css3-content/#content">http://www.w3.org/TR/css3-content/#content</a> for computation rules.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2926}),e[2927]=t({parent:e[2353],name:"box-shadow",flags:4,mods:0,cat:2,meta:{alias:"bxs",desc:`<p>Attaches one or more drop-shadows to the box. The property is a comma-separated list of shadows, each specified by 2-4 length values, an optional color, and an optional &#39;inset&#39; keyword. Omitted lengths are 0; omitted colors are a user agent chosen color.</p>
`,aliases:["bxs"]},id:2927}),e[2928]=t({parent:e[2927],name:"inset",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>Changes the drop shadow from an outer shadow (one that shadows the box onto the canvas, as if it were lifted above the canvas) to an inner shadow (one that shadows the canvas onto the box, as if the box were cut out of the canvas and shifted behind it).</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2928}),e[2929]=t({parent:e[2927],name:"none",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>No shadow.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2929}),e[2930]=t({parent:e[2353],name:"background-image",flags:4,mods:0,cat:2,meta:{alias:"bgi",desc:`<p>Sets the background image(s) of an element.</p>
`,aliases:["bgi"]},id:2930}),e[2931]=t({parent:e[2930],name:"none",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>Counts as an image layer but draws nothing.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2931}),e[2932]=t({parent:e[2353],name:"padding-right",flags:4,mods:0,cat:2,meta:{alias:"pr",desc:`<p>Shorthand property to set values the thickness of the padding area. If left is omitted, it is the same as right. If bottom is omitted it is the same as top, if right is omitted it is the same as top. The value may not be negative.</p>
`,aliases:["pr"]},id:2932}),e[2933]=t({parent:e[2353],name:"white-space",flags:4,mods:0,cat:2,meta:{alias:"ws",desc:`<p>Shorthand property for the &#39;white-space-collapsing&#39; and &#39;text-wrap&#39; properties.</p>
`,aliases:["ws"]},id:2933}),e[2934]=t({parent:e[2933],name:"normal",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>Sets &#39;white-space-collapsing&#39; to &#39;collapse&#39; and &#39;text-wrap&#39; to &#39;normal&#39;.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2934}),e[2935]=t({parent:e[2933],name:"nowrap",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>Sets &#39;white-space-collapsing&#39; to &#39;collapse&#39; and &#39;text-wrap&#39; to &#39;none&#39;.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:2935}),e[2936]=t({parent:e[2933],name:"pre",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>Sets &#39;white-space-collapsing&#39; to &#39;preserve&#39; and &#39;text-wrap&#39; to &#39;none&#39;.</p>
