`,imba:!0},id:3383}),e[3384]=t({parent:e[3380],name:"auto",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>As a maximum, identical to &#39;max-content&#39;. As a minimum, represents the largest minimum size (as specified by min-width/min-height) of the grid items occupying the grid track.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:3384}),e[3385]=t({parent:e[3380],name:"subgrid",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>Indicates that the grid will align to its parent grid in that axis.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:3385}),e[3386]=t({parent:e[3380],name:"minmax",flags:8192,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>Defines a size range greater than or equal to min and less than or equal to max.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:3386}),e[3387]=t({parent:e[3380],name:"repeat",flags:8192,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>Represents a repeated fragment of the track list, allowing a large number of columns or rows that exhibit a recurring pattern to be written in a more compact form.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:3387}),e[3388]=t({parent:e[2353],name:"list-style-position",flags:4,mods:0,cat:2,meta:{desc:`<p>Specifies the position of the &#39;::marker&#39; pseudo-element&#39;s box in the list item.</p>
`},id:3388}),e[3389]=t({parent:e[3388],name:"inside",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>The marker box is outside the principal block box, as described in the section on the ::marker pseudo-element below.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:3389}),e[3390]=t({parent:e[3388],name:"outside",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>The ::marker pseudo-element is an inline element placed immediately before all ::before pseudo-elements in the principal block box, after which the element&#39;s content flows.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:3390}),e[3391]=t({parent:e[2353],name:"font-feature-settings",flags:4,mods:0,cat:2,meta:{desc:`<p>Provides low-level control over OpenType font features. It is intended as a way of providing access to font features that are not widely used but are needed for a particular use case.</p>
`},id:3391}),e[3392]=t({parent:e[3391],name:"normal",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>No change in glyph substitution or positioning occurs.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:3392}),e[3393]=t({parent:e[3391],name:"off",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>Disable feature.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:3393}),e[3394]=t({parent:e[3391],name:"on",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>Enable feature.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:3394}),e[3395]=t({parent:e[2353],name:"contain",flags:4,mods:0,cat:2,meta:{desc:`<p>Indicates that an element and its contents are, as much as possible, independent of the rest of the document tree.</p>
`},id:3395}),e[3396]=t({parent:e[3395],name:"none",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>Indicates that the property has no effect.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:3396}),e[3397]=t({parent:e[3395],name:"strict",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>Turns on all forms of containment for the element.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:3397}),e[3398]=t({parent:e[3395],name:"content",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>All containment rules except size are applied to the element.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:3398}),e[3399]=t({parent:e[3395],name:"size",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>For properties that can have effects on more than just an element and its descendants, those effects don&#39;t escape the containing element.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:3399}),e[3400]=t({parent:e[3395],name:"layout",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>Turns on layout containment for the element.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:3400}),e[3401]=t({parent:e[3395],name:"style",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>Turns on style containment for the element.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:3401}),e[3402]=t({parent:e[3395],name:"paint",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>Turns on paint containment for the element.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:3402}),e[3403]=t({parent:e[2353],name:"background-position-x",flags:4,mods:0,cat:2,meta:{desc:`<p>If background images have been specified, this property specifies their initial position (after any resizing) within their corresponding background positioning area.</p>
`},id:3403}),e[3404]=t({parent:e[3403],name:"center",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>Equivalent to &#39;50%&#39; (&#39;left 50%&#39;) for the horizontal position if the horizontal position is not otherwise specified, or &#39;50%&#39; (&#39;top 50%&#39;) for the vertical position if it is.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:3404}),e[3405]=t({parent:e[3403],name:"left",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>Equivalent to &#39;0%&#39; for the horizontal position if one or two values are given, otherwise specifies the left edge as the origin for the next offset.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:3405}),e[3406]=t({parent:e[3403],name:"right",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>Equivalent to &#39;100%&#39; for the horizontal position if one or two values are given, otherwise specifies the right edge as the origin for the next offset.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:3406}),e[3407]=t({parent:e[2353],name:"transform-style",flags:4,mods:0,cat:2,meta:{desc:`<p>Defines how nested elements are rendered in 3D space.</p>
`},id:3407}),e[3408]=t({parent:e[3407],name:"flat",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>All children of this element are rendered flattened into the 2D plane of the element.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:3408}),e[3409]=t({parent:e[3407],name:"preserve-3d",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>Flattening is not performed, so children maintain their position in 3D space.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:3409}),e[3410]=t({parent:e[2353],name:"background-origin",flags:4,mods:0,cat:2,meta:{alias:"bgo",desc:`<p>For elements rendered as a single box, specifies the background positioning area. For elements rendered as multiple boxes (e.g., inline boxes on several lines, boxes on several pages) specifies which boxes &#39;box-decoration-break&#39; operates on to determine the background positioning area(s).</p>
`,aliases:["bgo"]},id:3410}),e[3411]=t({parent:e[2353],name:"border-left-style",flags:4,mods:0,cat:2,meta:{alias:"bsl",desc:`<p>Sets the style of the left border.</p>
`,aliases:["bsl"]},id:3411}),e[3412]=t({parent:e[2353],name:"font-display",flags:4,mods:0,cat:2,meta:{desc:`<p>The font-display descriptor determines how a font face is displayed based on whether and when it is downloaded and ready to use.</p>
`},id:3412}),e[3413]=t({parent:e[2353],name:"clip-path",flags:4,mods:0,cat:2,meta:{desc:`<p>Specifies a clipping path where everything inside the path is visible and everything outside is clipped out.</p>
`},id:3413}),e[3414]=t({parent:e[3413],name:"none",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>No clipping path gets created.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:3414}),e[3415]=t({parent:e[3413],name:"url",flags:8192,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>References a <clipPath> element to create a clipping path.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:3415}),e[3416]=t({parent:e[2353],name:"hyphens",flags:4,mods:0,cat:2,meta:{desc:`<p>Controls whether hyphenation is allowed to create more break opportunities within a line of text.</p>
`},id:3416}),e[3417]=t({parent:e[3416],name:"auto",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>Conditional hyphenation characters inside a word, if present, take priority over automatic resources when determining hyphenation points within the word.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:3417}),e[3418]=t({parent:e[3416],name:"manual",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>Words are only broken at line breaks where there are characters inside the word that suggest line break opportunities</p>
`,imba:!0},id:3418}),e[3419]=t({parent:e[3416],name:"none",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>Words are not broken at line breaks, even if characters inside the word suggest line break points.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:3419}),e[3420]=t({parent:e[2353],name:"background-attachment",flags:4,mods:0,cat:2,meta:{alias:"bga",desc:`<p>Specifies whether the background images are fixed with regard to the viewport (&#39;fixed&#39;) or scroll along with the element (&#39;scroll&#39;) or its contents (&#39;local&#39;).</p>
`,aliases:["bga"]},id:3420}),e[3421]=t({parent:e[3420],name:"fixed",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>The background is fixed with regard to the viewport. In paged media where there is no viewport, a &#39;fixed&#39; background is fixed with respect to the page box and therefore replicated on every page.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:3421}),e[3422]=t({parent:e[3420],name:"local",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>The background is fixed with regard to the element’s contents: if the element has a scrolling mechanism, the background scrolls with the element’s contents.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:3422}),e[3423]=t({parent:e[3420],name:"scroll",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>The background is fixed with regard to the element itself and does not scroll with its contents. (It is effectively attached to the element’s border.)</p>
`,imba:!0},id:3423}),e[3424]=t({parent:e[2353],name:"border-right-style",flags:4,mods:0,cat:2,meta:{alias:"bsr",desc:`<p>Sets the style of the right border.</p>
