`,imba:!0},id:3454}),e[3455]=t({parent:e[2353],name:"border-image",flags:4,mods:0,cat:2,meta:{desc:`<p>Shorthand property for setting &#39;border-image-source&#39;, &#39;border-image-slice&#39;, &#39;border-image-width&#39;, &#39;border-image-outset&#39; and &#39;border-image-repeat&#39;. Omitted values are set to their initial values.</p>
`},id:3455}),e[3456]=t({parent:e[3455],name:"auto",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>If &#39;auto&#39; is specified then the border image width is the intrinsic width or height (whichever is applicable) of the corresponding image slice. If the image does not have the required intrinsic dimension then the corresponding border-width is used instead.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:3456}),e[3457]=t({parent:e[3455],name:"fill",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>Causes the middle part of the border-image to be preserved.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:3457}),e[3458]=t({parent:e[3455],name:"none",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>Use the border styles.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:3458}),e[3459]=t({parent:e[3455],name:"repeat",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>The image is tiled (repeated) to fill the area.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:3459}),e[3460]=t({parent:e[3455],name:"round",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>The image is tiled (repeated) to fill the area. If it does not fill the area with a whole number of tiles, the image is rescaled so that it does.</p>
`,imba:!0},id:3460}),e[3461]=t({parent:e[3455],name:"space",flags:8,mods:0,cat:32,meta:{desc:`<p>The image is tiled (repeated) to fill the area. If it does not fill the area with a whole number of tiles, the extra space is distributed around the tiles.</p>
